0..77 Comment "// The members a data block writes, side by side, and what each arrow does. A"
78..151 Comment "// single shaft builds and a double shaft computes; a left head makes the"
152..208 Comment "// arrow invertible (`surface-lowering`, `module/data`):"
209..211 Comment "//"
212..287 Comment "//   `S : (x : Int) --> Int`       a constructor: builds a term of the sort"
288..369 Comment "//   `oper pred(x : Int) -> Int`    an operation: a term former the rules compute"
370..449 Comment "//   `rule P(S(x)) ==> x`           a rule: computes its left side to its right"
450..526 Comment "//   `rule x <=> S(P(x))`           an invertible rule: one term spelled two"
527..600 Comment "//                                  ways; the order chooses the direction"
601..679 Comment "//   `loop : Base <-> Base`         an invertible cell: adds a path at a point"
680..760 Comment "//   `loop : Base --> Base`         a directed cell: not minted, refused by name"
761..842 Comment "//                                  (`pathological/identity/directed-cell.gandr`)"
843..845 Comment "//"
846..916 Comment "// A rule collapses terms the constructors build, so the type is their"
917..994 Comment "// quotient; a cell adds a path between points the constructors build, so the"
995..1068 Comment "// paths at the point are the words over it. `Int` is presented by rules:"
1069..1149 Comment "// `S(P(x))` is `x`. `Circle` carries a cell: `loop` is apart from `here(Base)`."
1151..1228 Comment "/// The integers: two constructors that cancel, one rule written directed and"
1229..1307 Comment "/// one invertible, and an operation the rules compute. The directed rule runs"
1308..1385 Comment "/// `P(S(x))` to `x` and nothing to `P(S(x))`; the invertible rule is read in"
1386..1464 Comment "/// the direction the order admits, `S(P(x))` to `x`. The operation\'s own rule"
1465..1535 Comment "/// unfolds it to a predecessor, which the directed rule then cancels."
1536..1538 Other "@["
1539..1549 Other "normalizes"
1549..1550 Other "("
1550..1551 StringLit "\""
1551..1572 StringLit "pred(S(S(Z))) ~> S(Z)"
1572..1573 StringLit "\""
